-<body data-page="hpc2-founder" data-founder-publication="R2"><a data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.skip" class="public-skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div data-public-header-placeholder=""></div><main id="main" class="founder-r1"><section data-client-visual-hero="FOUNDER-HERO-001" data-founder-portrait-state="ASSET_VERIFIED" class="founder-r2-hero" data-founder-r1="S01" id="founder-s01"><picture class="founder-r2-hero-media" data-founder-image-state="ASSET_VERIFIED"><source media="(max-width:760px)" srcset="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/founder/PHIOS-FOUNDER-TERESA-LEE-PORTRAIT-CROP-v1.webp"><img data-founder-asset-id="FOUNDER-HERO-001" src="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/founder/PHIOS-FOUNDER-TERESA-LEE-HERO-v1.webp" width="1672" height="941" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Teresa Lee, Founder and Principal Architect of PHI OS." data-i18n-alt="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.portraitAlt"></picture><div class="founder-r2-hero-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="founder-r2-hero-content"><p class="founder-r2-eyebrow" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.eyebrow">Founder · PHI OS · Reality Navigation</p><h1><span data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.heroFirst">Answers are becoming easier to get.</span><span data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.heroSecond">The harder question is which answer actually belongs to your reality.</span></h1><div class="founder-r2-identity"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.navigation.identity">Teresa Lee</p><p class="founder-r2-role" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.role">Founder &amp; Principal Architect, PHI OS</p></div><p class="founder-r2-intro" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.intro">PHI OS began with a recurring question in real decisions: how can different sources help us see the same reality clearly?</p><nav data-i18n-aria-label="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.navLabel" class="founder-r2-hero-actions" aria-label="Founder introduction"><a href="/about/" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.why">Why PHI OS</a><a href="#founder-s08" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.origin">Founder &amp; Research Origin ↓</a></nav></div></section><section class="founder-r2-story" data-founder-r1="S08" id="founder-s08"><p aria-hidden="true" class="founder-r2-section-number">08</p><div data-founder-portrait-state="ASSET_VERIFIED" class="founder-r2-origin"><figure class="founder-r2-origin-media" data-founder-image-state="ASSET_VERIFIED"><img data-founder-asset-id="FOUNDER-PORTRAIT-001" src="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/founder/PHIOS-FOUNDER-TERESA-LEE-PORTRAIT-CROP-v1.webp" width="1122" height="1402" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Teresa Lee, Founder and Principal Architect of PHI OS." data-i18n-alt="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.portraitAlt"></figure><div class="founder-r2-origin-copy"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.eyebrow.0">Founder &amp; Research Origin</p><h2 data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.title.0">PHI OS did not begin as a technology idea. It began as a recurring problem in real decisions.</h2><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.navigation.identity">Teresa Lee</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.navigation.role">Founder &amp; Principal Architect, PHI OS</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.short_intro.0">PHI OS did not begin with a decision to build an AI platform and then search for a problem to solve.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.short_intro.1">It began with the same fracture appearing repeatedly across different areas of work and research.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.0">In financial planning, a decision is rarely only about numbers.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.1">Cash flow, assets, liabilities, family responsibilities, risk, time, and future objectives often exist together.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.2">In resource allocation and organizational restructuring, a plan that appears logical on paper may fail if it ignores people, structure, authority, execution capacity, or the external environment.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.3">In systems analysis, a conclusion that looks correct locally can produce a very different outcome when placed inside a larger structure.</p></div></div><div class="founder-r1-prose founder-r2-origin-continuation"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.4">Human reality makes the problem even more complex.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.5">A person can simultaneously hold professional advice, family views, personal intuition, historical experience, financial constraints, interpretive frameworks, and new changes in circumstance.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.6">None of these sources needs to be wrong.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.7">But they are often disconnected.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.8">The recurring question was never how to find one framework that would always be correct.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.9">It was:</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.10">What does a framework actually see?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.11">What does it leave out?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.12">What is its interpretation based on?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.13">And when reality changes, does the interpretation still hold?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.14">This is why seemingly distant fields became relevant to the same inquiry.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.15">Finance and resource allocation deal with real constraints.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.16">Organizational and systems work deal with structure and connection.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.17">Historical reading systems deal with patterns, timing, and meaning.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.18">Observation science deals with how information, evidence, and knowledge are formed.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.19">Artificial intelligence pushes all of these questions into a new stage: when generating and synthesizing answers becomes extremely fast and inexpensive, what capability becomes more important?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.20">PHI OS emerged from the convergence of those questions.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.21">It is not an attempt to prove that one framework is more correct than every other framework.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.22">Nor is it an attempt to build a system that knows every answer about a person’s life.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.23">Its purpose is closer to this:</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.24">to build an infrastructure in which different sources can be used without losing their identities;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.25">where interpretation can exist without automatically replacing fact;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.26">where unknowns can remain visible rather than being prematurely filled;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.27">where an earlier conclusion can be checked again as reality changes;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.28">and where a person can understand what their own decision is actually based on.</p></div><blockquote class="founder-r2-founder-quote" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.founder_quote.0">The problem I wanted to solve was not how to give people more answers. It was how to help them still see their reality clearly after they already have so many.</blockquote></section>
-<section class="vr2-story" data-ask-about-r1 id="why"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="About PHI OS" data-cx-zh="关于 PHI OS">About PHI OS</h2><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Connect sources, interpretations and lived experience while keeping their limits visible. Start from a question; choose what to bring into your reality." data-cx-zh="连接来源、解释与实际经历，同时保留各自边界。从问题开始，由你选择带入现实的资料。">Connect sources, interpretations and lived experience while keeping their limits visible. Start from a question; choose what to bring into your reality.</p></section>
- <section class="vr2-story" id="how"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Three ways to begin" data-cx-zh="三种开始方式">Three ways to begin</h2><ul class="ask-r1-graph"><li><a href="/knowledge/ask/" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Find an entrance" data-cx-zh="找到入口">Find an entrance</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Describe what you want to understand; choose a relevant function. Nothing is generated automatically." data-cx-zh="说出你想了解的事，再选择相关功能。不会自动生成报告。">Describe what you want to understand; choose a relevant function. Nothing is generated automatically.</p></li><li><a href="/knowledge/ask/?task=KNOWLEDGE_BASIC" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Understand knowledge" data-cx-zh="理解知识">Understand knowledge</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Read existing explanations and open their sources. Basic knowledge answers do not call an AI model." data-cx-zh="阅读已有解释并打开来源。基础知识回答不会调用 AI 模型。">Read existing explanations and open their sources. Basic knowledge answers do not call an AI model.</p></li><li><a href="/reality/" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Continue my reality" data-cx-zh="继续我的现实">Continue my reality</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Select your authorized material and current situation. Existing paid follow-up keeps its access and cost rules." data-cx-zh="主动选择已授权资料与当前处境。既有付费追问继续遵守其权限和成本规则。">Select your authorized material and current situation. Existing paid follow-up keeps its access and cost rules.</p></li></ul></section>
- <section class="vr2-story" id="start"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Independent perspectives, shared responsibility" data-cx-zh="独立视角，共同责任">Independent perspectives, shared responsibility</h2><ul class="ask-r1-graph"><li><a href="/perspectives/phi-configuration/">PHI Configuration · PHI 构型</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="A PHI OS model of personal structure, not a verified fact or capability score." data-cx-zh="PHI OS 的个人结构模型，不是已证实的事实或能力评分。">A PHI OS model of personal structure, not a verified fact or capability score.</p></li><li><a href="/perspectives/profile/">Profile · 个人画像</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Organize self-report, tasks and external assessments by their real sources." data-cx-zh="按真实来源整理自陈、任务表现与外部评估。">Organize self-report, tasks and external assessments by their real sources.</p></li><li><a href="/reality/" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Reality navigation" data-cx-zh="现实导航">Reality navigation</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Compare selected material with your current experience; no report is a required starting point." data-cx-zh="把主动选择的资料与当前经历对照；不强制先取得报告。">Compare selected material with your current experience; no report is a required starting point.</p></li></ul></section>
- <section class="vr2-story" id="faq"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Sources, privacy and responsibility" data-cx-zh="来源、隐私与责任">Sources, privacy and responsibility</h2><details><summary data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Do I need a report first?" data-cx-zh="必须先取得报告吗？">Do I need a report first?</summary><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="No. You can start from a public source or your current situation. Private records require your selection and server authorization." data-cx-zh="不需要。你可以从公开来源或当前处境开始。私有资料须由你选择，并经服务器授权。">No. You can start from a public source or your current situation. Private records require your selection and server authorization.</p></details><details><summary data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Does interpretation establish a fact?" data-cx-zh="解释会成为事实吗？">Does interpretation establish a fact?</summary><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="No. Sources, models and observations retain distinct labels and boundaries." data-cx-zh="不会。来源、模型与实际观察保留不同标签和边界。">No. Sources, models and observations retain distinct labels and boundaries.</p></details><a href="/privacy.html" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Privacy" data-cx-zh="隐私">Privacy</a></section><details class="vr2-story"><summary data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Read the accepted Founder publication in full" data-cx-zh="阅读已接受的 Founder 完整正文">Read the accepted Founder publication in full</summary><section class="founder-r2-story" data-founder-r1="S02" id="founder-s02"><p aria-hidden="true" class="founder-r2-section-number">02</p><h2 data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.title.0">The problem is no longer access to information.</h2><div class="founder-r1-prose founder-r2-problem-intro"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.0">Today, a person can search for information in seconds, ask an AI, watch expert commentary, read reports, compare perspectives, and draw on financial, relational, personal, symbolic, or professional frameworks.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.1">The problem is no longer simply whether an answer is available.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.2">The harder problem is that these answers come from different sources, use different methods, and describe different layers of reality. Some agree. Some conflict. Some remain relevant. Others have already been overtaken by events. Some are interpretations; others depend on facts that still need to be established.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.3">PHI OS begins at that point.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.4">It is not designed to become one more source of answers. It is designed to help a person bring information, interpretations, perspectives, and real-world conditions into one inspectable structure—so they can see what is happening now, what is actually known, what remains uncertain, and what any next step is based on.</p></div><blockquote data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.display_statement.0">We have more answers than ever. Reality has not become easier to judge.</blockquote><div class="founder-r1-prose"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.body.0">For much of the past, many decisions were difficult because information was scarce.</p>
+<body data-page="hpc2-founder" data-founder-publication="R2"><a data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.skip" class="public-skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div data-public-header-placeholder=""></div><main id="main" class="founder-r1"><section data-client-visual-hero="FOUNDER-HERO-001" data-founder-portrait-state="ASSET_VERIFIED" class="founder-r2-hero" data-founder-r1="S01" id="founder-s01"><picture class="founder-r2-hero-media" data-founder-image-state="ASSET_VERIFIED"><source media="(max-width:760px)" srcset="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/founder/PHIOS-FOUNDER-TERESA-LEE-PORTRAIT-CROP-v1.webp"><img data-founder-asset-id="FOUNDER-HERO-001" src="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/founder/PHIOS-FOUNDER-TERESA-LEE-HERO-v1.webp" width="1672" height="941" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Teresa Lee, Founder and Principal Architect of PHI OS." data-i18n-alt="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.portraitAlt"></picture><div class="founder-r2-hero-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="founder-r2-hero-content"><p class="founder-r2-eyebrow" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.eyebrow">Founder · PHI OS · Reality Navigation</p><h1><span data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.heroFirst">Answers are becoming easier to get.</span><span data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.heroSecond">The harder question is which answer actually belongs to your reality.</span></h1><div class="founder-r2-identity"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.navigation.identity">Teresa Lee</p><p class="founder-r2-role" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.role">Founder &amp; Principal Architect, PHI OS</p></div><p class="founder-r2-intro" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.intro">PHI OS began with a recurring question in real decisions: how can different sources help us see the same reality clearly?</p><nav data-i18n-aria-label="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.navLabel" class="founder-r2-hero-actions" aria-label="Founder introduction"><a href="/about/" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.why">Why PHI OS</a><a href="#founder-s08" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.origin">Founder &amp; Research Origin ↓</a></nav></div></section><section class="founder-r2-story founder-r3-research-start" data-founder-r1="S08" id="founder-s08"><p aria-hidden="true" class="founder-r2-section-number">08</p><h2 data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.title.0">PHI OS did not begin as a technology idea. It began as a recurring problem in real decisions.</h2><div class="founder-r1-prose founder-r3-research-prose"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.short_intro.0">PHI OS did not begin with a decision to build an AI platform and then search for a problem to solve.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.short_intro.1">It began with the same fracture appearing repeatedly across different areas of work and research.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.0">In financial planning, a decision is rarely only about numbers.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.1">Cash flow, assets, liabilities, family responsibilities, risk, time, and future objectives often exist together.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.2">In resource allocation and organizational restructuring, a plan that appears logical on paper may fail if it ignores people, structure, authority, execution capacity, or the external environment.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.3">In systems analysis, a conclusion that looks correct locally can produce a very different outcome when placed inside a larger structure.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.4">Human reality makes the problem even more complex.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.5">A person can simultaneously hold professional advice, family views, personal intuition, historical experience, financial constraints, interpretive frameworks, and new changes in circumstance.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.6">None of these sources needs to be wrong.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.7">But they are often disconnected.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.8">The recurring question was never how to find one framework that would always be correct.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.9">It was:</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.10">What does a framework actually see?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.11">What does it leave out?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.12">What is its interpretation based on?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.13">And when reality changes, does the interpretation still hold?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.14">This is why seemingly distant fields became relevant to the same inquiry.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.15">Finance and resource allocation deal with real constraints.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.16">Organizational and systems work deal with structure and connection.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.17">Historical reading systems deal with patterns, timing, and meaning.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.18">Observation science deals with how information, evidence, and knowledge are formed.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.19">Artificial intelligence pushes all of these questions into a new stage: when generating and synthesizing answers becomes extremely fast and inexpensive, what capability becomes more important?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.20">PHI OS emerged from the convergence of those questions.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.21">It is not an attempt to prove that one framework is more correct than every other framework.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.22">Nor is it an attempt to build a system that knows every answer about a person’s life.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.23">Its purpose is closer to this:</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.24">to build an infrastructure in which different sources can be used without losing their identities;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.25">where interpretation can exist without automatically replacing fact;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.26">where unknowns can remain visible rather than being prematurely filled;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.27">where an earlier conclusion can be checked again as reality changes;</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.body.28">and where a person can understand what their own decision is actually based on.</p></div></section>
+<section class="founder-r2-story" data-founder-r1="S02" id="founder-s02"><p aria-hidden="true" class="founder-r2-section-number">02</p><h2 data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.title.0">The problem is no longer access to information.</h2><div class="founder-r1-prose founder-r2-problem-intro"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.0">Today, a person can search for information in seconds, ask an AI, watch expert commentary, read reports, compare perspectives, and draw on financial, relational, personal, symbolic, or professional frameworks.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.1">The problem is no longer simply whether an answer is available.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.2">The harder problem is that these answers come from different sources, use different methods, and describe different layers of reality. Some agree. Some conflict. Some remain relevant. Others have already been overtaken by events. Some are interpretations; others depend on facts that still need to be established.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.3">PHI OS begins at that point.</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S01.lead.4">It is not designed to become one more source of answers. It is designed to help a person bring information, interpretations, perspectives, and real-world conditions into one inspectable structure—so they can see what is happening now, what is actually known, what remains uncertain, and what any next step is based on.</p></div><blockquote data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.display_statement.0">We have more answers than ever. Reality has not become easier to judge.</blockquote><div class="founder-r1-prose"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.body.0">For much of the past, many decisions were difficult because information was scarce.</p>
 <p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.body.1">Today, difficulty can come from having too much of it.</p>
 <p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.body.2">A person considering a career change may already have search results, AI conversations, industry news, personal reports, a partner’s opinion, financial numbers, past experience, and their own intuition. A relationship question may bring together psychological content, friends’ views, symbolic readings, social-media experiences, and professional advice.</p>
 <p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S02.body.3">Each source may contribute something useful.</p>
@@ -75,6 +72,46 @@
 <p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.28">Reality Navigation is not an attempt to know everything about a person.</p>
 <p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.29">It is an attempt to know, at a particular moment:</p>
 <p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.30">What do we actually need to know in order to understand this situation?</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.31"></p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.32"></p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.33"></p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.34"></p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.35"></p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.36"></p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.37"></p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.body.38"></p></div><figure class="founder-r1-figure" data-founder-asset-id="PLAN-CROSS-07"><a data-i18n-aria-label="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.figure" href="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/figures/Entrance/PHIOS-FIGURE-CROSS-DOMAIN-CONTEXT-LINKS-v1.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View full figure"><img src="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/figures/Entrance/PHIOS-FIGURE-CROSS-DOMAIN-CONTEXT-LINKS-v1.webp" width="1586" height="992" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Conceptual illustration: cross domain context links" data-i18n-alt="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.figures.CROSS-DOMAIN-CONTEXT-LINKS.alt"></a><figcaption><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S03.caption.0">Cross-domain context does not mean automatic data merging. Only information that is relevant to the current question, source-visible, and appropriately selected should enter the same Reality reading.</p><a href="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/figures/Entrance/PHIOS-FIGURE-CROSS-DOMAIN-CONTEXT-LINKS-v1.webp" class="founder-r1-link" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.navigation.full">View full figure</a></figcaption></figure></section>
+<section class="vr2-story" data-ask-about-r1 id="why"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="About PHI OS" data-cx-zh="关于 PHI OS">About PHI OS</h2><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Connect sources, interpretations and lived experience while keeping their limits visible. Start from a question; choose what to bring into your reality." data-cx-zh="连接来源、解释与实际经历，同时保留各自边界。从问题开始，由你选择带入现实的资料。">Connect sources, interpretations and lived experience while keeping their limits visible. Start from a question; choose what to bring into your reality.</p></section>
+ <section class="vr2-story" id="how"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Three ways to begin" data-cx-zh="三种开始方式">Three ways to begin</h2><ul class="ask-r1-graph"><li><a href="/knowledge/ask/" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Find an entrance" data-cx-zh="找到入口">Find an entrance</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Describe what you want to understand; choose a relevant function. Nothing is generated automatically." data-cx-zh="说出你想了解的事，再选择相关功能。不会自动生成报告。">Describe what you want to understand; choose a relevant function. Nothing is generated automatically.</p></li><li><a href="/knowledge/ask/?task=KNOWLEDGE_BASIC" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Understand knowledge" data-cx-zh="理解知识">Understand knowledge</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Read existing explanations and open their sources. Basic knowledge answers do not call an AI model." data-cx-zh="阅读已有解释并打开来源。基础知识回答不会调用 AI 模型。">Read existing explanations and open their sources. Basic knowledge answers do not call an AI model.</p></li><li><a href="/reality/" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Continue my reality" data-cx-zh="继续我的现实">Continue my reality</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Select your authorized material and current situation. Existing paid follow-up keeps its access and cost rules." data-cx-zh="主动选择已授权资料与当前处境。既有付费追问继续遵守其权限和成本规则。">Select your authorized material and current situation. Existing paid follow-up keeps its access and cost rules.</p></li></ul></section>
+ <section class="vr2-story" id="start"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Independent perspectives, shared responsibility" data-cx-zh="独立视角，共同责任">Independent perspectives, shared responsibility</h2><ul class="ask-r1-graph"><li><a href="/perspectives/phi-configuration/">PHI Configuration · PHI 构型</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="A PHI OS model of personal structure, not a verified fact or capability score." data-cx-zh="PHI OS 的个人结构模型，不是已证实的事实或能力评分。">A PHI OS model of personal structure, not a verified fact or capability score.</p></li><li><a href="/perspectives/profile/">Profile · 个人画像</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Organize self-report, tasks and external assessments by their real sources." data-cx-zh="按真实来源整理自陈、任务表现与外部评估。">Organize self-report, tasks and external assessments by their real sources.</p></li><li><a href="/reality/" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Reality navigation" data-cx-zh="现实导航">Reality navigation</a><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Compare selected material with your current experience; no report is a required starting point." data-cx-zh="把主动选择的资料与当前经历对照；不强制先取得报告。">Compare selected material with your current experience; no report is a required starting point.</p></li></ul></section>
+ <section class="vr2-story" id="faq"><h2 data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Sources, privacy and responsibility" data-cx-zh="来源、隐私与责任">Sources, privacy and responsibility</h2><details><summary data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Do I need a report first?" data-cx-zh="必须先取得报告吗？">Do I need a report first?</summary><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="No. You can start from a public source or your current situation. Private records require your selection and server authorization." data-cx-zh="不需要。你可以从公开来源或当前处境开始。私有资料须由你选择，并经服务器授权。">No. You can start from a public source or your current situation. Private records require your selection and server authorization.</p></details><details><summary data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Does interpretation establish a fact?" data-cx-zh="解释会成为事实吗？">Does interpretation establish a fact?</summary><p data-pis-copy data-cx-en="No. Sources, models and observations retain distinct labels and boundaries." data-cx-zh="不会。来源、模型与实际观察保留不同标签和边界。">No. Sources, models and observations retain distinct labels and boundaries.</p></details><a href="/privacy.html" data-pis-copy data-cx-en="Privacy" data-cx-zh="隐私">Privacy</a></section><section class="founder-r2-story" data-founder-r1="S07" id="founder-s07"><p aria-hidden="true" class="founder-r2-section-number">07</p><h2 data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.title.0">The more a system can connect, the more clearly it must show what each source can—and cannot—support.</h2><div class="founder-r1-prose"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.0">PHI OS can connect information from different domains, but connection must not erase the differences between them.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.1">This is one of the most important constraints in the system.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.2">A fact may come from an observed event or record.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.3">A financial number may come from account information or a calculation.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.4">A Profile result may come from a defined assessment or questionnaire.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.5">A professional judgment may come from a person who accepts responsibility within a specific scope.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.6">BaZi, Zi Wei, Astrology, I Ching, Tarot, and other methods provide a different kind of interpretive structure.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.7">AI can help organize, compare, explain, and connect these materials.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.8">But they do not become the same kind of evidence simply because they appear in one interface.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.9">PHI OS therefore needs to keep several questions visible:</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.10">Who provided this?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.11">What method produced it?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.12">What does it apply to?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.13">Is it presenting a fact or an interpretation?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.14">Was it reviewed by a person?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.15">Is it still current?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.16">Did the user choose to bring it into this question?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.17">And what is the system actually authorized to do with it?</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.18">These boundaries become more important as AI becomes more capable.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.19">A fluent answer can combine established facts, inference, interpretation, general knowledge, model synthesis, and unresolved uncertainty in a single paragraph.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.20">If the interface no longer distinguishes those layers, the user may experience one highly confident voice where several different kinds of claims actually exist.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.21">PHI OS should not work that way.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.22">AI can participate in reading reality.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.23">But AI should not automatically become the highest authority over reality.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.24">The ability to summarize financial information does not make it a financial adviser.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.25">The ability to interpret a symbolic method does not turn that interpretation into an established personality fact.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.26">And the ability to see several sources at once does not authorize a system to make a decision for the person when consent, evidence, or responsibility is insufficient.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.27">Professional participation also needs clear boundaries.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.28">Professional responsibility belongs to a specific person, service scope, and point in time—not to a generic “Professional” label.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.29">PHI OS is designed to preserve those relationships of responsibility rather than absorb them into a vague system authority.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.30">The platform can organize and present.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.31">A professional can judge within an appropriate scope.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.32">A method can offer a perspective.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.33">AI can assist interpretation.</p>
+<p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S07.body.34">But the person retains the decision.</p></div><div data-founder-portrait-state="ASSET_VERIFIED" class="founder-r2-origin founder-r3-research-profile"><figure class="founder-r2-origin-media" data-founder-image-state="ASSET_VERIFIED"><img data-founder-asset-id="FOUNDER-PORTRAIT-001" src="https://pub-1967bc5812ee4164b19a806fb1427021.r2.dev/images/founder/PHIOS-FOUNDER-TERESA-LEE-PORTRAIT-CROP-v1.webp" width="1122" height="1402" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Teresa Lee, Founder and Principal Architect of PHI OS." data-i18n-alt="hpc2Destinations.founder.humanPresenceR2.portraitAlt"></figure><div class="founder-r2-origin-copy"><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.eyebrow.0">Founder &amp; Research Origin</p><p class="founder-r3-profile-name" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.navigation.identity">Teresa Lee</p><p data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.navigation.role">Founder &amp; Principal Architect, PHI OS</p></div></div><blockquote class="founder-r2-founder-quote" data-i18n="hpc2Destinations.founder.publication.S08.founder_quote.0">The problem I wanted to solve was not how to give people more answers. It was how to help them still see their reality clearly after they already have so many.</blockquote></section>
